# Manager brief — <project>

**Outcome:** <what must be true when this operation is right>.

**Direction:** Read `<vision>` and `<contracts>` first. Work comes only from a
named contract gap or steward feedback; the steward alone ratifies, sets
priority, or stops work.

**Operation facts:** Repository: `<path>`; integration branch: `<branch>`; queue:
`<source>`; intended project width: `<n>`; authorized resource cap: `<fact or none>`;
continuation record: `<plan/return-record path>`; next checkpoint: `<time/event>`.
Transferred execution scope/state: `<exact scope and receipt, or none>`.
Resource caps constrain capacity; transferred scope changes local readiness.

**Boundaries:** For each produced interface, record producer, consumers,
interface decision owner within agreed direction, version or fixture, incoming
dependency, consumer acceptance owner and check, and residual destination.
Local success, consumer-accepted, and product-accepted are distinct.

**Execution:** Keep nonconflicting work moving. An ended lane or failed
applicable consumer check has a finite integration priority before a conflicting
refill; record temporary under-width, its budget, and the next repair. Re-run
actual integrated acceptance and record revision, environment, and output. For
an installed consumer, include a consumer journey; otherwise record `N/A — no
installed consumer applies`.

**Wait and transfer:** Declare health, checkpoint, deadline, and a missed-boundary
route before passive waiting. A tool or guard refusal stops immediately; do not
try another tool around it. Transfers record offered/accepted/declined or
unaccepted/returned/reintegrated plus exact scope, revision, evidence or gaps,
execution and reintegration owners, decision rights, receipt, and checkpoint.
Exported is not accepted; stop duplicate local execution after accepted transfer
or an explicit steward stop. An unaccepted offer remains locally accountable;
absence of a receipt never overrides a stop.

**Amplifier preflight only:** Compose Converge, activate `/mode
converge-manager`, then verify the actual mode, required tools, skills, agents,
identity, queue, repository, capacity, and continuation path. Do not invent an
`--mode converge-manager` flag. A full conversation does not provide missing
capabilities.